condition_name: Syncope (Fainting)
condition_slug: syncope-fainting
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Loss of consciousness and postural tone as a result of diminished cerebral blood flow. This can result from Vaso-vagal attack or cardiac causes; prolonged standing; severe emotional disturbance; sight of blood (e.g. witnessed by medical student for the first time in theatre) The more severe form is associated with various heart diseases: Arrhythmias (especially complete heart block); Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy; 'Heart attack' (myocardial infarction); Atrial myxoma; Aortic stenosis; Dissecting aneurysm other causes; Pulmonary embolism; Vertebro-basilar insufficiency; Subclavian steal syndrome; Carotid sinus pressure and rarely Migraine headache"
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: syncope
    features[7]: Sudden fall to the ground with loss of consciousness,Cold extremities,Bluish discolouration of extremities (cyanosis),Pulse irregularities (or pulselessness),Hypotension (or unrecordable blood pressure),Fainting induced by pressure on the neck,"Fainting induced by coughing, micturition"
investigations[4]: Electrocardiography,Echocardiography,"Neuro-imaging: CT scan, MRI, carotid Doppler",Random blood sugar
treatment:
  goals[3]: Restore circulation and ensure brain perfusion by elevating the legs to increase venous return,Identify cause and treat accordingly,Prevent recurrence
  non_drug[1]: "Physiotherapy: pressure stockings"
  drug[2]: "Specific treatment for cardiac arrhythmias: Please refer to cardiologist","If hypotensive, give pressor agents"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: "Aspirin and other NSAIDs: use with caution in patients with history of dyspepsia, and in asthmatics"
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[5]: Epilepsy,Myocardial infarction,Stroke,Aortic dissection,Conversion disorder
complications[3]: Cerebral hypoxia/anoxia resulting in brain damage,Stroke,Sudden death
prevention[5]: Avoid prolonged standing,Treat underlying cardiac disease,Avoid dehydration or excessive fluid loss,Ensure adequate calorie and avoid prolonged fasting,Use medication as prescribed by physicians and avoid overdosage to compensate for missed doses
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null